-- author  : @marwahaha
-- created : 2026-10-24T14:43:48.386745+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/e30e58d9-f76d-498b-8bb0-7c4a3412645b
-- title:
--   Masses of successful recorded observation traces
-- statement:
--   Fix a ground size $n$, rank parameter $r$, Boolean subset oracles, a schedule $s$, phase $j$, a current annealing cursor $c$, a fixed Boolean prefix $u$, and a suffix length $t$. Let $m=s.\mathrm{observations}$ and let $\mathbf x=(x_0,\ldots,x_{m-1})$ be a vector of paired states. The actual recorded-trace mass is
--   $$
--   K(\mathbf x)=2^{-t}\sum_{v\in\{0,1\}^t}
--   \mathbf 1\{\text{the restart followed by recorded observation returns exactly }\mathbf x\}.
--   $$
--   Both operations use the tape $u\mathbin{+\!\!+}v$ defaulted to false, the supplied current tables and cursor, activity $s.\rho^j$, and the supplied current weights. The terminal observation cursor may be any successful one; aborts contribute zero.
--
--   For a finite Markov chain $P$ on paired states, let $\nu(z)$ be the actual capped-restart endpoint mass on the same finite suffix experiment. The comparison path mass is
--   $$
--   R_P(\mathbf x)=
--   \sum_{\substack{y_0,\ldots,y_m\\(y_0,\ldots,y_{m-1})=\mathbf x}}
--   \nu(y_0)\prod_{i=0}^{m-1}P(y_i,y_{i+1}).
--   $$
--   The final unrecorded transition is summed out. Neither definition conditions on successful execution or replaces the restart marginal by a stationary law.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/SuccessfulPrefixRecordedTraceSubkernel.lean#L28-L44

